  SUM OF SQUARES IDENTITY (n=4)
========================================================================

  Example fiber overlap class distribution:
    Overlap class: size 2
  Σ (count)² = 4, should relate to 2^{m-1} = 32

  Within each fiber: 2 tilings, 2 overlap configs → bijection
  (One tiling per overlap, by construction)

  THE WIGGLY GRAPH within a fiber is the COMPLETE GRAPH K_2
  (Every pair of tilings with the same boundary+apex is wiggly-connected)
  Wiggly degree: 1 (= fiber_size - 1 = 2^{C(n-2,2)} - 1)

